From e13b652f1eca625cda864a0c12499f56702232d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:24:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci: run light PR checks and completion aggregates on the
 ci-fast lane [daveey]

Eleven short jobs (6-83 s, git/python3/jq/setup-pm only) asked for
[self-hosted, hermes-hub] and queued up to 50 min behind full suites while
ci-fast runners sat idle (PR #266). Move them to [self-hosted, ci-fast]
with unchanged job/check names: All required checks pass (v2), CI timing
report, check-common-ancestor, check-attribution, uv.lock check, icon
freshness, package-lock diff, prompt surface summary, and the supply-chain
scan/dep-bounds/aggregate jobs (timeouts 15 -> 10 min, the lane cap).

fork-ci-runner.sh now pins every admitted fast-lane job back to ci-fast,
so a re-run after an upstream merge cannot return them to the heavy pool.
Evidence table in .github/FAST-LANE.md.
---
